nd step  prepare a presentation prepare slides  prepare a document and then of course in  the end there's the presentation itself  where the pages are being presented and  are being discussed in the meeting so  let's go here step by step step number  one what happened here well of course  often information has been gathered by  colleagues other sources maybe some  expert interviews that this person will  have conducted you do this together with  the team and then you derive the results  together with your colleagues on the  topics at hand second step when you  structure then all the analyses into  some type of presentation document of  course hopefully you apply the good  slight writing principles the  communication techniques top-down  communication  principle that we talk about so  frequently here on this channel if all  of this says nothing to you i will link  a playlist above here where you will  read about more of these topics watch  videos on exactly this last but not  least there's a presentation of course  often the team lead will deliver this  presentation him or herself in front of  the senior leadership of the  organization and now once again i want  you to pause the video and think about  that thinking about this approach will  this likely be successful will this  likely lead to a good result  and my humble opinion in my experience  is no this will not work right because  what is the problem if you do this this  process often leads to negative outcomes  as also shared in the initial example  why because the team did not manage to  align the results with all the key  stakeholders of the organization  alignment one of the most important  topics in every big corporate in  consulting for sure it is a topic so  common so important in consulting that  it is literally a meme here my friends  at consulting humor prepared this little  quote  just had a meeting to a line on how we  would align with the client during our  weekly alignment meeting right alignment  a