ure that they  feel like they have been part of the  solution that they feel like it was  maybe even their idea what you proposed  in the end this often goes a long way  next never never never walk into meeting  with your senior leaders and letting  them see the document the first time but  what i mean is that you properly take  the time to in the one or two weeks  before this is very important meeting  you meet with all these people one on  one and you guide them through the  document if it's not the final document  because it's not ready yet then at least  the rough outline the key results that  you want to share and you ask them for  their feedback you ask them for their  guidance and this is of course  especially important also in consulting  and potentially especially challenging  and consulting because they are not only  you need to align the documents with  your clients but you also need to align  all the key documents with your internal  leadership and this can be quite  challenging because often you end up  going in circuits right so you create a  document align it with a client then you  take the document show it to your  partner and actually your partner  disagrees the partner i think no this is  not what you can do so you turn around  the document then you go back with this  document to the client and then the  client says no i disagree right and then  this can go really in circuit so that's  often quite a pain especially as a  project lead to moderate all this and  then last but not least for this  presentation in front of the senior  leaders very carefully think about  whether you are really the best person  to present it and of course i understand  that maybe you think ah it would be  great for myself to get this visibility  get the spotlight present in front of  all these senior leaders but sometimes  it might make more sense for potentially  a person more senior than you to present  it this is actually even more important  than in professional servi